{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Shortest paths from one or more sources: for each reached vertex, its distance, its parent and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the edge from the parent (a forest when there are several sources)."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ShortestPathTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Distance","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Distance","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The first relaxation to a vertex’s final distance wins. So "},{"code":"parent(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shortest-path predecessor of "},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" settled first. Vertices at equal distance settle in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unspecified order, so when several vertices at the same smallest distance lead to "},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" along"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shortest paths, which one is the parent is unspecified. Among parallel edges from the parent,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the parent edge is the cheapest, and the first in "},{"code":"outEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order among equals."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A tree holds a copy of the graph, so looking a vertex up never hashes on a representation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with cheap vertex indices. While the tree is alive, the next mutation of the original copies","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it; a tree of a graph about to change should be read and dropped first.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With several sources, each starts at distance zero ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".one"},{"type":"text","text":" over a semiring) with no parent."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Dijkstra’s algorithm and breadth-first search never improve on that, so a source keeps no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parent even when another source reaches it. Bellman–Ford treats the sources as one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"super-source: a negative path from one source to another improves the second, which then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has that distance, a parent and a path from the first."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Over a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SelectiveSemiring"},{"text":" a distance is the ⊗-product of a path’s weights, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"best by the natural order ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<"},{"text":", and a vertex is reached exactly when its distance is not ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".zero"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Not ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": two correct trees can choose different parents on ties.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ShortestPathTree"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:13ShortestPaths0A8PathTreeV","modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ShortestPathTree","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ShortestPathTree","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree.swift#L29","fileName":"ShortestPathTree.swift"}},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/sources"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/distance(checkedTo:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/distance(to:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/distance(toIndex:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/hasPath(checkedTo:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/hasPath(to:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parent(checked:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parent(of:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parent(ofIndex:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestPathTree\/parentEdge(checked:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/document